{
  "root_node": "model.stg_customers",
  "cause": "code_change",
  "action": "patch",
  "evidence": "The failing not_null test on stg_customers.market_segment reports 288 nulls. The raw.customer table has 1500 rows, with exactly 288 rows where c_mktsegment = 'MACHINERY'. The stg_customers model defines market_segment as nullif(trim(c_mktsegment), 'MACHINERY'), which converts every 'MACHINERY' value to NULL. Thus the nulls are introduced by the model's SQL, not by missing data upstream. The fix is to adjust the model (e.g., remove the nullif or map 'MACHINERY' to a proper segment) so that market_segment is never NULL."
}
